## Maximum Subarray

### Approach — Kadane's Algorithm

--  Keep a max variable to store the current subarray sum.
--  Keep a maxSub variable to store the maximum sum found so far.
--  Add every element to max.
--  Update maxSub with the current max.
--  If max becomes negative, reset it to 0 because a negative sum will only reduce the sum of the future subarray.
--  Initialize maxSub with Integer.MIN_VALUE so that arrays containing only negative numbers are handled correctly.

## Complexity : 
--  Time Complexity : O(n)
--  Space Complexity : O(1)

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        int max = 0;
        int maxSub = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for(int right = 0; right < nums.length; right++) {
            max += nums[right];
            maxSub = Math.max(max, maxSub);
            if(max < 0) {
                max = 0;
            }
        }    
        return maxSub;  
    }
}
